<onlyinclude>'''Open-source intelligence''' (OSINT) is the collection and analysis of publicly or commercially accessible information to answer a defined intelligence question. It differs from covert acquisition and from merely collecting links.

== Explanation ==
Researchers may compare official records, public reports, maps and photographs to verify an event. Reliable work preserves sources, checks dates and locations, distinguishes observations from interpretations and avoids exposing private people unnecessarily. Open-source intelligence is unrelated to whether software has an open-source license.

